do and as we know  zoro is going to join the fighting again  soon with the help of medical science  we're on a roll people the only question  is how many more times will the tables  turn and how close are we chapter wise  to the end of this conflict we jump to  the castle interior third floor and by  the way i'm so glad we're told the  position because i would not remember if  we weren't we joined the ninja battle  between rhizo and fukurokuju we get some  comedic naruto vibes during this battle  as rhizo uses clone jutsu and fuku  fights with his earlobes that's such a  bizarre odo way of fighting and it is  reminiscent to me of how jurai uses his  hair in battle in naruto but obviously  earlobes are funnier it's so funny how  easy fuku finds out who the real one is  by simply saying he's clinging to a  ghost and then the real rhizo responds  saying are you talking about odensama  the earlobe strikes and rhizo gets  earlobe whipped i must say these are  probably the most opie earlobes i've  ever seen fuku then tells raizo that he  wasn't suited to be a ninja because he  wore his heart on his sleeves while a  ninja is supposed to be more stoic but  it looks like fuku hasn't watched naruto  or he would have realized that rhizo has  his own ninja way believe it amid the  humor though we do get a great moment  where ryzel says that the day the day of  the execution they all cried laughed and  died alongside odin thus they are all  ghosts bent on fulfilling odin's dream i  really like their code of honor and  friendship it's heartwarming and  inspiring to see we get shots of all the  scabbards some on the ground while  others are still fighting rhizo then  mentions that it's not just out of duty  that they are fighting unlike fuku they  fight because of that emotional bond  that they had with odin so rather than a  hindrance emotions and bonds can be a  source of motivation and power nothing  groundbreaking here especially for  shonen anime but i appreciate it  nonetheless rhizo goes on to say that it  doesn't matter if they die they have to  see this through to the end or they  won't be able to rest in other words if  they fail to try to carry out their  mission that would be worse than death  to them no matter if they got to keep  their lives i love to see these kinds of  manly sentiments being shared finally  rhizo tells him that tonight will mark  the end of the orochi and kaido reign  and there will be a brilliant dawn  tomorrow with momo as shogun and as we  got from last chapter momo will probably  be an adult by the morning so it  wouldn't be weird to see him take the  role on at all it's so crazy to consider  that luffy and friends may overcome my  uncle crew and even to individual yonko  but things are definitely looking good  right now knock on wood and rizal's  words are getting me even more pumped up  we also get to drop in on killer vs  hawkins it's clear that killer's on the  offensive and going through a bunch of  hawkins so-called meat shields he's  exhausted by the thought of how many he  still has thankfully hawkins says he  doesn't have any left but things take a  very interesting turn when he says  killers should consider not how many are  left but whose life is currently  standing in for the life of hawkins we  then jump to big mom vs law and kid  another very hyped matchup and against  the yonko they definitely need all of  their faculties and luck too but  unfortunately hawkins was talking about  kid and kid starts noticing that  something stabbed him so yeah now for  killer to beat hawkins it seems like  he'll have to cut down kid first albeit  indirectly this makes hawkins a very  tricky fighter obviously killer would  never kill kid so he may have to find a  way to restrain hawkins or find a  workaround otherwise hawkins may take  out killer and although killer is  definitely cool he's enough of a side  character for him to possibly be taken  out right here so you never know what's  gonna happen things could have been much  worse if hawkins didn't finally admit  that kid is his current meat shield but  he's thinking about himself and wants  killer to agonize over fighting back  this is the best way to assure his own  victory while letting killer kill kid  would not have been best for him  necessarily but it would have been the  better move for the beast pirates as a  whole as far as side fights go this is  definitely an interesting one and i look  forward to seeing what happens and how  it plays out as killer points out  hawkins is twisted and that works really  well for antagonists like him not gonna  lie then we get to the meat and potatoes  of the chapter if you will we see an  amazing panel of king and queen  absolutely towering over everyone else  in the panel people are begging marco to  help and in a pretty crazy panel he  looks to be down for the count as it  said that he's reached his limit  interestingly enough oda did say in a  question corner that marco's  regeneration has its limits and i  believe that simply means when his  stamina runs out he can't use the  regeneration anymore however the  question is if his stamina is at zero  right now or not in the meantime the  all-stars are unleashed and people  believe they're going to destroy the  whole floor pretty soon that's how crazy  destructive they are sanji tells them to  get zorro out of the way obviously he  used the loving nickname moss head  instead of zoro but there's no way that  they'll actually be taking zoro away  from the battle the reason sanji said  that is because it looked like the shot  wasn't working zoro was still in  excruciating pain in fact it's taking  longer to take effect because he's in  such bad shape it's so crazy that he'll  have to deal with double this pain  afterwards not to mention the pain he'll  accumulate during the rest of the war  it's absolutely insane and such a zorro  situation to be in i think we may have  the makings for a moment that may really  rival the famous nothing happen moment  as they're waiting for my boy zorro the  legend to heal sanji continues to kick  around queen and i love these matchups i  wasn't sure with jimbei in the picture  who sanji would be fighting but i'm glad  it worked out like this interestingly  enough king is actually worried about  zoro and tells people to find him and  finish him off because the straw hats  are trying some weird healing method  he's very machiavellian in the sense  that he wants him dealt with before he  recovers he's not just thinking oh he's  not a threat i'll deal with him easily  which i respect i like to see our straw  hats being taken so seriously by such  strong opponents it shows how far we've  come in the meantime pero sparrow is  aiming at sanji with an arrow he's  especially mad at him because he feels  like if he married pudding then they  never would have joined forces with the  beast pirates so it's not just business  but personal for pero sparrow it's funny  how he calls him a germa reject but even  funnier how he gets smacked around by  nekomamushi who has arrived to avenge  pedro i really think that this avenged  pedro storyline is hilarious i wonder if  this is just going to keep haunting pero  sparrow wherever he goes for the rest of  his life because pedro decided to blow  himself up then just as it looks like  zoro is done for because the people  carrying him are surrounded and king is  right in front of them marco comes to  the rescue the yonko commander hasn't in  fact been taken out so easily which is  quite the relief he successfully blocks  king's divine flame attack with a smile  on his face to boot then we get some  interesting dialogue where marco says he  used to hear rumors about a certain fire  conjuring race that lived on top of the  red line and calls king king of the  flames but of course marco won't be the  one to fight him to the end because he's  more here to assist rather than to hog  the spotlight as the all-stars prepare  to turn to marco again marco says he  gives and that he's done his part i like  this because a marcos still comes off as  a strong dude who wasn't defeated by  king and queen in a definitive way and b  he's allowing our main guys to take the  spotlight namely zorro easily one of my  favorite characters marco even says it's  time for the stars to take stage as  zorro comes out of the bandages and you  know he adjusted his glasses while he  was at it i love the fact that in front  of the all-stars he pretty much called  zorro and the straw hats the true stars  way back i think we all saw zoro  battling king and i love to see it  finally here we get an amazing moment  and panel where zoro and sanji attack  together side by side one kicking queen  and the other slicing king we're told  that the two wings are in action which  is hype for sanji and zorro who both  managed to keep their wing status in the  evolving crew and i just can't get over  it it's so great to see these two  fighting together side by side against  the all-stars no less kaido's two  strongest fighters the bystanders go  crazy like me as they scream the straw  hats are amazing and we get another  great moment and i know i keep saying  that but this chapter is full of them  zorro says hey curly brows if we win  this and then sanji interrupts him to  finish the thought saying i know it'll  finally be in sight luffy becoming king  of the pirates goosebumps people this is  so epic right now it's making me want to  cry tears of awesomeness we have reached  the climax of this arc where these two  will take on the all-stars and luffy is  just about to meet up with kaido again  for the last time during this war i  could not have been more satisfied with  this chapter as always let me know your  thoughts about the chapter and what  you're most looking forward to seeing  next who was your mvp i gotta go with my  boy zoro for taking the pain for  returning in such a spectacular fashion  and for cutting down king i'm not saying  king is down for long but still it was  an epic panel if i could pick two mvps  at once if that's a thing then the duo  of sanji and zorro definitely gets it  their dynamic and role in this chapter  was just amazing and that is it for this  one as always thank you so much for  joining me in discussing another amazing  chapter if you do enjoy seeing these  one-piece chapter reviews and want to  keep them coming the best you could do  is channel the pyroking within and smash  that like button if you haven't make  this the video you subscribe and this is  crucial hit that notification bell to  turn on all notifications or you will  miss future one piece videos hitting the  like button and subscribing is very  pirating energy while not doing so as  very orochi energy just saying and while  you wait for the next chapter to drop  feel free to check out my giant and  growing one piece playlist that includes  exclusive videos on the yonko warlords  and most recently all nine mythical zone  users and their powers explained like i  said at least three of those mythical  zones will probably surprise you let me  know if they do in the comments of that  video you can find all of these videos  and more in my one piece playlist link  to that is in the description and until  next time see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you

